    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer - Register now at SherryFitz.ie\n\nAn exceptionally charming, thatched cottage, located in the heart of historic Keshcarrigan along the route of the Shannon-Erne Waterway at Lough Scur and just south of Keshcarrigan Lough.\n\nThis Period property, which may have built in the early 18thC, enjoys a prominent position in the village adjacent to local amenities including cafe/shop, 2 pubs serving food, a marina with boats & waterside trails.\n\nOriginally constructed as an office and residence for the manager of the local Butter Market and weighbridge, it most probably formed part of the Lough Scur and Laheen Estate owned by the Peyton family.\n\nThe area is steeped in mythology, evolving history and significant archaeological sites and conveniently located just 14km from Carrick-on-Shannon, 11km to Leitrim Village, 9km to Drumshanbo & 13km from Ballinamore \n\nAn idyllic holiday home, artists retreat or short let accommodation for anyone exploring the many riches of this region. \n\nViewing highly recommend and by appointment only - please contact Liam Farrell of Sherry FitzGerald Farrell."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nLiving Room - 3.95m x 3.45m\n'Stone Flag' ceramic floor tiles, exposed beam ceiling, open fireplace with oak mantel, traditional lamp fitting, electric storage heater, sash window with metal pole and drapes, door to outside.\n\nDining Room - 3.63m x 3.34m\n'Stone Flag' ceramic floor tiles, entrance door, sash window with metal pole & drapes. Feature open fireplace with exposed stone and brick surround, traditional crook & solid fuel stove, pendant lamp fitting. Rustic wall shelves, electric storage heater, stairs to upper floor.\n\nKitchen - 2.79mx 2.68m\n'Stone Flag' floor tiling, fitted storage and cupboard units with electric hob & ovens, tiled splashbacks, window x 2, original Jubilee solid fuel range, rustic globe light fitting, integrated Whirlpool fridge freezer, T&G pine ceiling, electric storage heater.\n\nBathroom - 2.62m x 2.17m\nFloor & wall tiling, shower enclosure with electric shower & chrome corner basket, chrome & globe wall lamps, glass shelf, chrome fittings, electric wall heather, wc & whb.\n\nBedroom One - 3.71m x 2.59m\nCarpet, window, chrome wall lamps, power points.\n\nBedroom Two - 3.79m x 3.16m\nCarpet, sash window with pole & drapes, wall lamp, power points.\n\nExternal - \n:* Natural stone wall road boundary with front and side entrances, steel gates to gravel drive and parking apron. * Large, lock up garage with concrete floor, side walls and original stone rear wall- excellent storage with Beko washer & dryer, electric water heater, shelving, power points. * Slipway to canal which links Keshcarrigan Lough and Lough scur. Access to village park.* Lovely, enclosed, mature garden to side with horse chestnut, fuchsia and various other plantings - a very pleasant space.* A rare opportunity to acquire a unique and special residence in the heart of unspoilt South Leitrim.\n\nAdditional - \n:These particulars have been prepared by Sherry FitzGerald Farrell and whilst every care has been taken to ensure that these are accurate and correct, we are not responsible for any errors, omissions, inaccuracies, if the property is let, sold or withdrawn from sale or if it is not suitable for your purpose. These particulars are for information only and are given under the strict understanding that they do not form part of any contract. Neither whole nor any part of this document or any reference thereto may be included in any public document, circular or statement nor published without the written consent of Sherry FitzGerald Farrell.\n\n"
      },
